 # Update Rules

-Review and evolve card-text rules without conducting an interactive interview. Never use `AskUserQuestion` or ask a rule-decision question in chat. The Markdown review file is the only decision channel: write every ruling question and every possible reusable new pattern there, stop without polling the file, and wait for the user to edit it. When the user later says `continue`, reopen the associated review file and immediately implement its completed answers without another approval round.
+Questions live in shared-template HTML. Answers return as copied clipboard summary. Never use `AskUserQuestion`; never ask decisions directly in chat. Generate once; stop; apply complete pasted summary without second approval.

